# Copy to .env and fill in — same convention as api/.env.example.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* is required for a var to be readable in client-side/browser code — Next.js
# only inlines env vars into the browser bundle when they carry this prefix. Server-only code
# (Server Components, Route Handlers) can read unprefixed vars too, but there are none of
# those here yet.
#
# If the team later adds a real Cloudflare Workers binding (an R2 bucket, KV, D1 — not just a
# plain string like this one), that specifically needs .dev.vars (or wrangler.jsonc), since
# only Cloudflare's own binding system creates those objects — a plain .env var can't.

# NEXT_PUBLIC_* is inlined at BUILD time, so these must be set wherever
# `opennextjs-cloudflare build` runs. Setting them as Worker runtime vars in the Cloudflare
# dashboard does nothing — the value is already baked into the browser bundle by then.

# finance-tracking-api — local mock server by default (see api/README.md).
# Deployed: https://finance-tracking-r0hw.onrender.com/v1
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:4000/v1

# Supabase Auth — used only for the "Continue with Google" redirect
# (src/lib/auth/supabaseOAuth.ts). No anon/publishable key is needed here: the browser never
# calls Supabase's data APIs, it just carries the resulting session token to
# POST /auth/login/supabase, and the API verifies it with its own key.
# Local stack default below; deployed: https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54321
